00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:01.981
The way that Perry talks about it,
it was actually Kathleen

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:05.385
who was the brains of the operation,
whereas her brother was more like the face

00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:06.319
of the resistance.

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:07.887
And Kathleen explains that she did

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:11.758
terrible things but did wind up
accomplishing all their goals.

00:03:11.758 --> 00:03:12.659
But her leadership,

00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:15.595
her decisions are what allowed them
to actually overthrow Pedro.

00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:17.397
And the whole vibe
that you're meant to get from her

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:20.500
character is that compared to him,
she's hardcore militant.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:24.204
She employed every dirty trick
in the book, did all kinds of dark stuff

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:26.506
that would normally haunt you
for the rest of your life.

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:30.543
They do a pretty good job of telegraphing
her tragic end in the episode,

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:34.514
like she has so many conversations about
how she wants to get revenge on Henry.

00:03:34.514 --> 00:03:36.516
When Joel was trying
to be so understanding,

00:03:36.516 --> 00:03:38.551
you clearly see the direction
her character is going.

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:40.853
Oh, she's definitely going to die
some horrible death.

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:42.722
But this is meant to be
the reason in present day

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:45.792
that Perry, the other hunters,
allow her to lead their group

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:48.695
because she's the one that
got the job done overthrowing Phaedra.

00:03:48.895 --> 00:03:51.064
And it all went down so recently.

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:53.700
Also, big Easter Egg for the Last of US
video game.

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:55.702
Perry is played by the same actor

00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:58.571
who did The voice for Joel's brother
Tommy, in the game.

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:01.507
He's one of many video game cameos
seen so far.

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:03.643
We'll see more of those in later episodes.

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:07.080
Just to explain the timeline, though,
Henry and Sam have only been on the run

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.982
for a short while in present day,

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:11.684
so the Hunters just got done
overthrowing Phaedra.

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:14.020
And when she's interrogating
the federal collaborators

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:16.823
at the beginning of the episode,
that's only 11 days ago.

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:22.028
So all these riots this just happened in
while that was all going down, she swore

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:25.598
revenge on Henry because he was forced
to sell out Kathleen's brother,

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:29.602
Brian, to Phaedra to obtain
leukemia medicine for his brother Sam.

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:32.772
He gave Phaedra, the leader, quote
unquote, of the resistance.

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:36.776
Kathleen implies that they tortured
and killed Brian in front of her eyes,

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:39.178
and it either drove her mad
or maybe she'd always been

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:41.114
just a little bit darker, gotten darker

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:44.350
because of what had happened
under federal rule for the past 20 years.

00:04:44.584 --> 00:04:48.354
As Henry explains that Phaedra had been
so terrible, it turned the inhabitants,

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:52.358
like the hunters here of Kansas City,
into the quarantine zone, into animals.

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:55.061
And when they overthrew Phaedra,
instead of doing what

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:56.996
normal people would do,
like pat each other on the back

00:04:56.996 --> 00:05:00.800
and try to make an even better version
of society, it just drove them to an even

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:01.301
darker place.

00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:04.370
They got even more about like,
violence begets more violence.

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.239
Abuse begets more abuse.

00:05:06.239 --> 00:05:10.376
As if life under Phaedra turned normal
people into monsters, into the hunters,

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:14.247
because they're meant to be like a dark
mirror faction to the Fireflies faction,

00:05:14.247 --> 00:05:16.983
even though the fireflies
also do a lot of terrible stuff too.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.318
There were a couple larger

00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:21.821
and smaller changes to the video games
for the Hunters storyline.

00:05:22.055 --> 00:05:23.222
One of the bigger ones was

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:26.759
what happened to the infected
after the fungus initial outbreak

00:05:27.026 --> 00:05:30.863
on the show many years ago,
before the insurrection, Phaedra drove

00:05:30.863 --> 00:05:32.832
the infected underground
and trapped in there.

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:35.134
So in present day,
you never see any of them above ground,

00:05:35.368 --> 00:05:38.137
which is why so many of them come
bursting out of the underground tunnels

00:05:38.137 --> 00:05:40.406
at the end of the episode,
like an infected pinata

00:05:40.707 --> 00:05:41.874
during the beginning of the episode

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:44.277
when they're rioting
after getting rid of Phaedra.

00:05:44.277 --> 00:05:46.579
Kathleen's speech later
reinforces the whole idea

00:05:46.579 --> 00:05:49.482
that violence begets more violence. Abuse
begets more abuse.

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:52.852
When you see the hunters
start abusing the federal agents,

00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:55.855
they start torturing and killing them,
hanging them up all over the place.

00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:56.656
In Kathleen,

00:05:56.656 --> 00:05:59.192
ordering the summary execution
of all the collaborators

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:01.427
after lying to them,
saying that they would get trials.

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:05.198
But to be fair, she did imply
that they would die no matter what.

00:06:05.198 --> 00:06:07.500
Like, we'll give you trials,
but you know how that's going to go.

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:11.537
So if her ironic delivery of the line
wasn't clear, everything's great now.

00:06:11.537 --> 00:06:14.173
Kansas City is free. Clearly,
everything is not great.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:15.007
It's just meant to be

00:06:15.007 --> 00:06:18.111
another example of how people are
just as bad as the infected,

00:06:18.211 --> 00:06:20.613
which is also a reference
to an Easter egg for later

00:06:20.613 --> 00:06:22.982
in the game for the ish character,
which I'll talk about

00:06:23.116 --> 00:06:24.384
because it's a very special moment.

00:06:24.384 --> 00:06:25.651
It's like one real small.

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:29.021
No, but it's this huge side
story in the game, this huge back story.

00:06:29.255 --> 00:06:31.924
There's moments like that
all over the Last of US episodes.

00:06:31.924 --> 00:06:32.492
We're like this

00:06:32.492 --> 00:06:36.062
tiny little thing in the background
has like this ten minute backstory to it.

00:06:36.229 --> 00:06:39.832
We see Henry using the chaos to try and
run to the doctor's hiding spot with Sam.

00:06:39.832 --> 00:06:43.302
One of the big changes here from the game
is that Henry and Sam were not originally

00:06:43.302 --> 00:06:45.405
from the same city
as the Hunters in on the show.

00:06:45.405 --> 00:06:47.607
It was also Pittsburgh,
and apparently the showrunner

00:06:47.607 --> 00:06:49.442
just really hates Pittsburgh
for some reason.

00:06:49.442 --> 00:06:53.246
Don't know why, but that's why he made
the city Kansas City end of the game.

00:06:53.246 --> 00:06:55.515
Sam isn't deaf
and he doesn't have leukemia.

00:06:55.515 --> 00:06:58.284
He's like a normal little kid
that Henry's trying to take care of.

00:06:58.551 --> 00:07:01.921
They also didn't have the whole
Kathleen versus Henry back story, too.

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:04.056
That was completely brand
new for the episode.

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:06.759
Kathleen herself
was not a character from the games,

00:07:06.993 --> 00:07:10.596
but in the game, just like the show,
they were still trying to escape the city

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:11.931
they had come through
and they were just trying

00:07:11.931 --> 00:07:14.200
to make their way west
to the other fireflies.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:17.570
On the show, though they weren't
specifically looking for other fireflies,

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:20.106
they were just looking
to get West in the game.

00:07:20.106 --> 00:07:23.376
The reason why Henry was so afraid
of the hunters and wanted to avoid them

00:07:23.443 --> 00:07:26.012
is because he thought
that they would just kill Sam

00:07:26.012 --> 00:07:28.681
